{"author":{"id":"7c5527b9befade3b1be0c1d677ac996815288d8332f34269730a5b81425ee5be"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791208890,"nonce":"RO+v91b+SquLnBc/cwcKhIrPwFI=","metadata":{"github-url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/40","origin":"github","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"I_kwDOULtcMc8AAAABVItLvQ","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:labels":"","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:number":"40","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:status":"open","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"98ed91225b8db9bd2aa1348349739ccd37578e0471200b49a161ac1393bad0d3","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:title":"[REFACTOR](Build) Remove pnpm and template leftovers, clean up Docker/nginx config","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/40"},"title":"[REFACTOR](Build) Remove pnpm and template leftovers, clean up Docker/nginx config","message":"**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\nThe build, deployment and repo config still carry Quasar-template and copy-paste leftovers. Each one is small, but together they make it hard to tell what is load-bearing.\n\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\n\n**Package manager: npm only**\n- [ ] Delete `frontend/pnpm-workspace.yaml`. The project uses npm and `package-lock.json`.\n- [ ] Drop `pnpm` and `yarn` from `engines` in `frontend/package.json`, and narrow `node` to the version pinned in `.nvmrc` (#39).\n- [ ] Fix the template metadata in `package.json`: `description` (\"Web app for vps-mitsi exhibition around  data\") and `productName` (trailing space).\n- [ ] `Makefile`: `install` should run `npm ci`, not `npm install`.\n- [ ] Add `node_modules/` to the root `.gitignore`. A root `node_modules/` was committed once and removed in `bfd7a02`.\n\n**`frontend/quasar.config.ts`**\n- [ ] Remove the unused template sections: `ssr`, `pwa`, `cordova`, `capacitor`, `electron` (including `appId: 'tech4dev-hosm'`, copied from another project), `bex` and the commented-out examples.\n- [ ] Keep only what the SPA uses.\n\n**`.github/workflows/pages.yml`**\n- [ ] Drop the `404.html` SPA-fallback step. The router uses hash mode (`vueRouterMode: 'hash'`), so deep links never reach the server.\n- [ ] Use `node-version-file` instead of `lts/*` (see #39).\n\n**Docker and nginx: depends on #38**\nIf #38 deletes the Docker path, this section becomes \"delete the files\". If the image is kept, align it with `EPFL-ENAC/co2-calculator` `frontend/Dockerfile` and `frontend/nginx.conf`:\n- [ ] **Layer order:** the `Dockerfile` copies the whole context before `npm ci`, so every source change reinstalls every dependency. Split it into stages: `COPY package.json package-lock.json`, `RUN --mount=type=cache,target=/root/.npm npm ci --ignore-scripts`, then `COPY . .` and `npm run build`.\n- [ ] **`.dockerignore`:** add one covering `node_modules`, `dist`, `.quasar`, `tests`, `.git` and editor files.\n- [ ] **Unprivileged runtime:** use `nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:stable-alpine-slim` (non-root, port 8080) with `apk upgrade --no-cache`, and add a `HEALTHCHECK` plus a `/healthz` endpoint.\n- [ ] **Delete `entrypoint.sh`:** it writes an `env.js` with `API_URL`, `API_PATH` and `AUTH_CLIENT_ID`, which the app never loads, and it's the only reason the image installs `bash`. Use the base image's default `CMD`.\n- [ ] **Fix caching in `nginx.conf`:**\n  - HTML is sent with `Cache-Control: public` and `expires -1y`; it should be `no-cache, must-revalidate`.\n  - Unhashed public files (`favicon.png`, `epfl.svg`) are cached `immutable` for 365 days, so a replaced file stays stale for a year.\n  - Make only content-hashed assets immutable and everything else `no-cache`, as co2-calculator does.\n\n**Branches**\n- [ ] Delete remote branches already merged into `dev`: `9-feat/export-import-json`, `dev1`, `feat/components-improvements`, `feat/results-page-charts`, `fix/cleanup-1`, `fix/remove-dead-files-while-keeping-kube-deploy-scripts`.\n- [ ] Decide on the unmerged `feat/20-results-report` and `fix/cleanup-2`.\n- [ ] Turn on \"Automatically delete head branches\" in the repo settings (currently off).\n\n**Docs**\n- [ ] Update both READMEs after the above (they still mention `stage`, the legacy `env.js` and `npm run format` staging files).\n\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\nLeave the template config in place \"in case\". That's speculative (YAGNI), and git history already keeps it.\n\n**Additional context**\nRaised in an architecture review of `dev` at `b35fc8c`. The ESLint template globals (Cordova, Capacitor, BEX, `ga`) are handled in #39.","files":null}]}